  "query_preview": "..\n(Sunday night through next Friday)\nIssued at 1024 PM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nA warming trend will begin this weekend through the middle of next \nweek with the building of an upper level ridge over the four \ncorners. The warming trend will primarily be due to the lack of \ncloud cover even though low level winds will continue to be out of \nthe east. Winds will return to the southwest as lee troughing \nestablishes itself. The upper level ridge will begin to break down \ntowards the middle of the week as a series of short wave troughs \nenter into the Pacific Northwest. Stronger lee troughing late in the \nweek will bring temperatures back up above seasonal averages.",
